## Rules

1. **One Checklist Step at a time** — never work on multiple in parallel.
2. **One commit per Checklist Step** — after Tester PASS. If `git status` shows nothing to commit although Refactorer reported "Step N done", that is a failure (see On Failure). Do not batch commits.
3. **Subagents by exact name** — `architect`, `refactorer`, `verifier`, `tester` so Cursor routes correctly. Subagent definitions: `.cursor/agents/`.
4. **One version bump per PR** — the Finalize step bumps `app/system/config.php` exactly once per Roadmap Step / PR. Subsequent mini-loop fix commits (Final Test mini-loop, Bugbot quick-peek mini-loop) on the same PR/branch **must not** trigger another `chore(release): bump version to ...` commit. The CHANGELOG-NEW.md section for the already-bumped version is amended in place to include the mini-loop changes; the ROADMAP header pointer stays on the same version. Rationale: the PR is one logical release unit. Re-bumping mid-review wastes commits, confuses readers of `git log`, and creates a fictitious version that was never tagged.

## Early Push (after all Checklist Steps committed, before Final Test)

Orchestrator (no subagent):

1. **Push** — `git push -u origin HEAD` from the feature branch.
2. **PR creation** — `gh pr create` with the `<!-- metadata -->` block (labels, milestone, `closes`). Use the GitHub Issue number from the invocation (`GitHub Issue: #XXX`). Include `Closes #XXX` in PR body AND in the metadata `closes:` field. See `push.mdc` § PR Metadata + `github-labels.mdc`.

This early push triggers CI (PHP Quality workflow) and Cursor Bugbot review. The Final Test step waits on those checks; the Bugbot peek runs after Final Test PASS.

## Final Test (after Early Push)

Tester runs in parallel: (a) `gh run watch` on the four PHP Quality CI jobs, (b) the 3 Playwright E2E specs locally. See `tester.md` § End-of-ticket tests for exact commands.

## Bugbot Quick-Peek (non-blocking, after Final Test PASS)

Two `gh api` calls. The review object itself only carries marketing text in its `body` ("Cursor Bugbot has reviewed your changes and found N potential issue(s)") — the **actual issue details (file, line, description) live in the review's inline comments**, fetched via a second call.

```bash
# 1. Latest Cursor-Bugbot review (commit SHA + review id)
LATEST=$(gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/$PR/reviews \
  --jq '[.[] | select(.user.login == "cursor")] | last')
REVIEW_ID=$(echo "$LATEST" | jq -r '.id // empty')
REVIEW_SHA=$(echo "$LATEST" | jq -r '.commit_id // empty')

# 2. Inline comments of that review (the actual findings)
COMMENTS=$(gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/$PR/reviews/$REVIEW_ID/comments \
  --jq '[.[] | {path, line, body}]')
COUNT=$(echo "$COMMENTS" | jq 'length')
```

Decision matrix:

- **No Cursor-Bugbot review yet** (`LATEST` empty) → proceed (Bugbot still working; the user reviews remaining findings manually before merging).
- **Review present, COUNT == 0** → proceed (Bugbot ran and flagged nothing, regardless of the body's marketing text).
- **REVIEW_SHA == HEAD, COUNT > 0** → mini-loop (Refactorer → Verifier → Tester → push fix → re-run Final Test → re-peek). Pass `COMMENTS` verbatim to the Refactorer as the fix list.
- **REVIEW_SHA != HEAD, COUNT > 0** → **delegate to Verifier** with the inline comments list (`COMMENTS`), `REVIEW_SHA`, and `HEAD` SHA. Verifier statically checks each comment to determine whether its specific issue has been resolved by any commit in `<REVIEW_SHA>..HEAD` (see `.cursor/agents/verifier.md` § Stale-Bugbot Check). Verifier output: PASS (all issues resolved) → proceed to Finalize. FAIL (one or more still present) → mini-loop with the still-present comments as Refactorer input.

NEVER wait for Bugbot to finish (Pro tier can take ~15 minutes). The user reviews remaining findings manually before merging.

**Why two API calls and not one:** The review's `body` field is human-friendly summary text ("found 1 potential issue") and intentionally lacks file/line precision. The actionable detail — what to fix — sits in the per-file inline comments attached to that review. Reading only `body` would force the Verifier to grep blindly across the whole codebase; reading the comments gives him exact `path:line` targets.

**Why the stale-SHA branch is not "blind proceed":** Earlier versions of this workflow treated stale-SHA Bugbot reviews as "the bug is probably already fixed by a later commit" and proceeded silently. That assumption is false — a later commit can fix an unrelated bug while leaving the Bugbot-flagged one untouched. The Verifier check above closes that loophole at near-zero token cost (one static code read per comment).

## Finalize (after Bugbot peek → proceed)

Orchestrator (no subagent) executes the relevant items of **push.mdc**:

1. **Branch documentation** — Create `migration-docs/branches/{task-name}.md` documenting:
   - All changes made (files, what changed, why)
   - Breaking changes for extensions (if any)
   - Test results summary (CI run reference + local E2E results)
   - Referenced **Roadmap Step X.Y** and GitHub Issue
   - PR number (now known from Early Push)
     Use existing files in `migration-docs/branches/` as reference for format/style.
2. **Version bump** — `.cursor/skills/version-bump/SKILL.md`
3. **CHANGELOG-NEW.md** — group all commits from this Roadmap Step
4. **ROADMAP update** — `.cursor/ROADMAP.md` (Header pointer, this step's row Status `⏳` → `✅`, Audit `⏳` → `🛡️`, **PR `-` → `#YYY`**, plus Phase 1 audit closures per `push.mdc`)
5. **Push** (second push) — updates the PR with the finalize commits.
6. **Do NOT merge** — user reviews and merges.

## On Failure (CRITICAL — do not self-fix)

The Orchestrator NEVER fixes code, reads files to understand errors, or runs tests to verify fixes. On ANY failure:

| Failure                                              | Action                                                                                                                                       |
| ---------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Refactorer reported done but tree clean**          | Re-delegate to **refactorer**: "Ticket: …, Checklist Step N. No changes detected on disk. Re-execute and emit changed files."                |
| **Verifier FAIL**                                    | Pass feedback to **refactorer**: "Ticket: …, Checklist Step N. Verifier feedback: [paste FAIL output verbatim]. Delegate to **refactorer**." |
| **Tester FAIL**                                      | Pass feedback to **refactorer**: "Ticket: …, Checklist Step N. Tester feedback: [paste FAIL output verbatim]. Delegate to **refactorer**."   |
| **Refactorer cannot fix** (architecture issue)       | Escalate to **architect**: "Ticket: …, Checklist Step N. Issue: [one line]. Delegate to **architect**."                                      |

After any fix: restart the loop from **verifier** (not from commit), then **tester**, then commit. Never amend commits yourself; let the refactorer produce clean changes, then commit normally.
